# Force LF line endings for all text files under site/ regardless of the checkout platform's
# core.autocrlf setting, so an editor on Windows cannot reintroduce CRLF through a commit.
# This consolidates the narrower rules that used to live here (site/**/*.g.cs, highlight.css,
# site/content/*.md); those patterns are subsets of the ones below and are no longer listed
# separately.
site/**/*.cs text eol=lf
site/**/*.razor text eol=lf
site/**/*.html text eol=lf
site/**/*.css text eol=lf
site/**/*.json text eol=lf
site/**/*.csproj text eol=lf
site/**/*.md text eol=lf
site/**/*.txt text eol=lf
site/**/.editorconfig text eol=lf
site/**/_headers text eol=lf

# CI sources eng/ci-assert.sh (". eng/ci-assert.sh") rather than executing it, and a CRLF
# checkout would corrupt that under bash: the trailing \r becomes part of the last token on
# every line, breaking function definitions and comparisons in ways that are hard to trace back
# to line endings. This repo-wide *.sh pattern covers eng/*.sh (including eng/ci-assert.sh), but
# NOT the extensionless eng/hooks/pre-push, which stays unspecified under this rule.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Committed baselines of generated source (see GeneratedSourceSnapshot). LF because the emitter picks
# its line endings from Environment.NewLine, so a Windows run produces CRLF and would otherwise
# rewrite every baseline on save. The comparison normalizes line endings anyway; this keeps the
# committed bytes stable so the diff stays reviewable, which is the only reason these are committed.
#
# -linguist-generated because the emitted text opens with `// <auto-generated/>`: without this GitHub
# collapses these files in a diff, and a collapsed diff defeats the point of committing them.
tests/BlazorCompose.Compiler.Tests/Snapshots/*.expected.cs text eol=lf -linguist-generated
